+# check-change, Step 3 Layer 2 - category: harness. PR #891, issue 875, base plan/788/base (5b1f0d81b37f).
+# Files graded: core/components/plays/shape-plan/SKILL.md, reference/ice.md, stop-condition.yaml.
+# Rule kept: no principle below rests on a file this branch adds or rewrites.
+pr: 891
+issue: 875
+category: harness
+base: plan/788/base
+severity_taxonomy: .garura/project/issues/875/context/memory/standards/rules/pr.md
+grounding_status: available
+
+principles:
+  - id: G1
+    principle: "A change to what a play guarantees is made in its ICE, and the compiled part is compiled again; the compiled part records the ICE fingerprint so the two never drift apart unseen."
+    source: "git show plan/788/base:docs/standards/harness-standard.md, principle 4 (cites ADR 027); CLAUDE.md 'Play Pipeline Rules' (intent change goes ICE -> /edit-play)"
+  - id: G2
+    principle: "Delivery work items are marked in the tracker by the issue type field, with no label; the Epic stands for one Slice and the Story for one Feature."
+    source: "git show plan/788/base:docs/adr/048-the-product-model-and-the-work-are-two-layers.md, Decision 1 and 3; git show plan/788/base:.garura/user-provided/managing-work.md ('Type lives in the type field', 'No labels, for now'); base shape-plan ice.md C13"
+  - id: G3
+    principle: "The tracker type used for the Epic must be a type the organization really has. On the base ref the organization had no Epic type, so the Epic was filed as Feature (#818 decision 5)."
+    source: "git show plan/788/base:.garura/project/issues/818/context/decisions.md, decision 5; git show plan/788/base:.garura/user-provided/managing-work.md lines 57-62. External check, read-only: GitHub GraphQL organization(login:intent-driven-ai).issueTypes now lists Business Intent, Feature, Story, Bug, Chore, Spike and Epic (all enabled)."
+  - id: G4
+    principle: "The shaping loop is /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval; /shape-plan makes one epic per slice and one story per feature and writes only the plan file, epics and stories."
+    source: "git show plan/788/base:docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 2-3"
+  - id: G5
+    principle: "Build the eval first: the check that proves a change is done is built before the change and fails against today's code."
+    source: "git show plan/788/base:docs/standards/harness-standard.md, principle 5"
+
+conformance_passes:
+  - "G1: the intent change (epic type Feature -> Epic in C13, F11, REC11, S1, D4, Context) is in reference/ice.md and SKILL.md in the same commit (71c1788f). SKILL.md's recorded fingerprint sha256:84f437cd... equals the sha256 of ice.md at the branch head (checked with shasum). The ICE-source rule holds. Whether /edit-play was the tool that ran cannot be seen from the diff; the content and fingerprint agree."
+  - "G1/G2: the SKILL.md description, Step 6 write text, SE-15, the F11 row and the ICE agree with each other; stop-condition.yaml D4 and ice.md D4 carry the same wording. No leftover 'epic type Feature' text in the three files."
+  - "G3: the base committed record said the org had no Epic type; the tracker now has it, and issue #875 says it was added on 2026-10-25. The new rule is grounded in the live tracker, not in branch prose. Old decision 5 is named as replaced in ice.md Context, so the superseded source is not left silent."
+  - "G2/G4: the change touches only the type name. The play->agent->skill->script wiring, the single pinned checkpoint, the write guard (D5) and the find-before-make rule are unchanged."
+
+findings:
+  - id: H1
+    severity: P4
+    severity_note: "No pr.md row matches a missing scenario; P4 is the closest bucket (tech-debt / nit, surfaced only in evidence). Not a blocker."
+    file: core/components/plays/shape-plan/reference/ice.md
